Subject: [PATCH] Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the core is Lichii nx2
 c363fafe26, with its patch series 0016-0144

The Eglantine submodule moves from d2eaae4 (Lichii nx2 of 9 Nov) to c363fafe26 (Lichii nx2 of 22 Nov,
https://github.com/zortos293/Lichii). tools/eglantine-patches holds the series EglantinePS5's build applies
on it: 62 patches, 0016 to 0144 (it was 19). Every patch opens with a paragraph saying what it changes and
why. The newer ones carry the Switch 2 side's memory and stability work: guest memory read through while it
is packed, the texture cache's give-back (2-frame age, a staged then full sweep while a write waits), shader
programs and pipeline records kept small, the descriptor tables grown as used, the kernel's page managers
committed where pages are handed out, render targets that cannot go back to 1x no longer stretching the
picture, the give-back's mode and wait from Playtendoh's settings. Patches that nx2 took in were dropped,
the rest refreshed on it. tools/eglantine-patches-pending lost the ones nx2 now has. The core's host
regression tests (headless/nx2-core-check) follow the new core.

