+A draw whose index buffer the device has no memory for is left out (GraphicsPipeline's configure fails, as for a draw without a pipeline) instead of ending the session: UpdateIndexBuffer finds it through FindBindingBuffer (0104), leaves the index binding empty, marks it dirty so the next draw asks again, and TakeRefusedIndexBuffer tells the pipeline before it binds anything. Ocarina of Time ended loading Castle Town on the PS5 on a 13 KiB index range (0111's log named UpdateIndexBuffer), with the shared 12 GiB full.
+
