+GpuSplit::RequestBetweenEntries: any thread can have the back thread run a function once, at its next step between entries while it works through them (never while it is quiet, when the front may use the scheduler), with BackWorking to tell whether it does. For the PS5's give-back of graphics memory (headless/main.cpp): queued after the work before it, the pass waited behind a full queue until a write of the game's memory found no block and the session ended (Ocarina of Time loading Castle Town, 20 Nov: not one pass in two sessions, the thread asking for it waiting in the queue).
+
+diff --git a/src/video_core/gpu_split.cpp b/src/video_core/gpu_split.cpp
